<name>New York City: The Park Five (5.0 mi)</name>
<description>DRAFT route. Not an official Nike route. Check it on the ground before you rely on it.</description>
<Style id="route"><LineStyle><color>ff2b39c0</color><width>5</width></LineStyle></Style>
<Placemark><name>New York City: The Park Five (5.0 mi)</name><styleUrl>#route</styleUrl>
<LineString><tessellate>1</tessellate><coordinates>-73.9593,40.78446,0 -73.95727,40.78708,0 -73.95623,40.78898,0 -73.95546,40.79099,0 -73.95505,40.79251,0 -73.95691,40.79362,0 -73.9595,40.79436,0 -73.96116,40.79336,0 -73.96338,40.79111,0 -73.96629,40.78744,0 -73.968,40.78477,0 -73.97011,40.78141,0 -73.97182,40.77873,0 -73.97452,40.77583,0 -73.97722,40.77293,0 -73.97834,40.77043,0 -73.97849,40.7688,0 -73.97707,40.76757,0 -73.97502,40.76672,0 -73.97309,40.76698,0 -73.97194,40.76904,0 -73.97099,40.77161,0 -73.96963,40.7738,0 -73.96829,40.77515,0 -73.96672,40.77619,0 -73.96518,40.77894,0 -73.96335,40.78114,0 -73.9616,40.78211,0 -73.9593,40.78446,0</coordinates></LineString></Placemark>
<Folder><name>Landmarks</name>
<Placemark><name>1. Engineers&#x27; Gate</name><description>Start and finish at East 90th Street and Fifth Avenue, the classic meeting point for New York runners.</description><Point><coordinates>-73.9593,40.78446,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>2. The Reservoir</name><description>A 1.58-mile cinder track circles the water. The short route cuts along its north side on the bridle path.</description><Point><coordinates>-73.96216,40.78721,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>3. The Pool</name><description>A quiet pond below the North Woods, just after the 102nd Street Cross Drive brings you to the west side.</description><Point><coordinates>-73.96116,40.79336,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>4. Delacorte Theater</name><description>The open-air home of free Shakespeare in the Park every summer.</description><Point><coordinates>-73.97011,40.78141,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>5. Strawberry Fields</name><description>The memorial to John Lennon. The short route turns east here across the 72nd Street Cross Drive.</description><Point><coordinates>-73.97452,40.77583,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>6. Tavern on the Green</name><description>The New York City Marathon finishes on West Drive right beside it.</description><Point><coordinates>-73.97722,40.77293,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>7. Wollman Rink</name><description>The southern end of the loop, with the Midtown skyline behind it.</description><Point><coordinates>-73.97502,40.76672,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>8. Bethesda Terrace</name><description>The fountain and arcade at the heart of the park, on the short route.</description><Point><coordinates>-73.97241,40.77474,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>9. Cat Hill</name><description>The one real climb on the way home. A bronze panther watches from the rock on your left.</description><Point><coordinates>-73.96672,40.77619,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>10. The Obelisk</name><description>An Egyptian obelisk behind the Metropolitan Museum of Art. Half a mile to the finish.</description><Point><coordinates>-73.96335,40.78114,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
